From 3863c8e5d5240b570da687e98b04e067874b96eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 11:07:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat: sparse .forge/config.yaml writer + forge gate/role
 verbs

Add lib/config-writer.js, a sparse read-modify-write for the
schema-validated .forge/config.yaml surface (array key-paths so gate
ids containing dots are never split). Two thin verbs ride it:

- `forge gate <enable|disable> <gate-id>` -> workflow.gates.<id>.enabled
  (consumed by the shipped applyEnabledConfig reader; forge options
  gates --json reflects it with zero new read code).
- `forge role <role> --use <skill> [--ideology <name>]` ->
  roles.<role>.skill / roles.<role>.ideology.

runtime-graph.js gains an additive, backward-compatible `roles` section
(sibling to workflow.gates) plus applyRoleConfig with OPEN-WORLD skill
validation: role names are the closed STAGE_IDS set, but the bound
skill/ideology names are validated only as non-empty strings and never
against the PLAN_SUBSKILL enum (which stays scoped to
planning.template.partialInvocation). forge options gains a `roles`
collection so `forge options roles --json` reflects resolved bindings.

Write-time validation: unknown gate id, unknown role, or unresolvable
skill (no SKILL.md under .skills/ > skills/) errors before any write,
never mid-run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
